<!--
    GH-1343. Stage P9, cast insertion (p9_emit/coreaction_casts.rs
    get_input_cast_store, p9_emit/kuna_floatstore.rs). Strict fix, no option.

    A pointer whose other stores are integers (clang stores each 1.0f constant
    as the bit pattern 0x3f800000 from an integer register) is typed as a
    pointer to unknown bytes. Upstream needs no cast to store any value into
    unknown bytes, so the float a vstr / movss / str s0 writes printed as
    `v1[2] = a0 * a1 + 0.5f;` with `unsigned int *v1`: kuna declares unknown
    bytes as an integer, and in C that assignment converts the float
    numerically (1.5f stores 1, not 0x3fc00000). The store now goes through a
    pointer to the value's own type, `*(float *)&v1[2] = ...`, which is the bit
    copy the instruction makes. The integer stores keep their bit patterns.

    Pass 1 is raw Thumb (clang 14 -O2, thumbv7em-none-eabihf, fpv4-sp-d16)
    linked at 0x8000010, reading the matrix pointer from a global at
    0x20000000:

        movw r0,#0; movt r0,#0x2000; ldr r0,[r0]
        vmul.f32 s2,s0,s1; vmov.f32 s4,#0.5; mov.w r1,#0x3f800000
        vadd.f32 s2,s2,s4; vsub.f32 s0,s0,s1
        str r1,[r0]; str r1,[r0,#16]; str r1,[r0,#32]
        vstr s2,[r0,#8]; vstr s0,[r0,#24]; bx lr

    Passes 2 and 3 load floatstore.c built by clang 14 -O2 for x86-64 (movss)
    and AArch64 (str s0), from kuna-analysis's fixtures (floatstore.provenance).
-->
